{
  // The ONLY project that type-checks `test/` and `scripts/`.
  //
  // The root `tsconfig.json` excludes `**/*.spec.ts`, so `npm run typecheck`
  // returns exit 0 with the entire suite hard-broken — a removed interface
  // field, a changed method signature, a renamed export all pass it. And the
  // specs are NOT type-checked when they run either: `npm test` loads them
  // through `ts-node/register/transpile-only` (see `package.json`), which strips
  // types without checking them. So a spec with a type error runs, and can pass.
  // This project is therefore not a faster version of a check that happens
  // anyway — it is the only type check the specs get. (This comment used to say
  // the opposite, that specs load "without `transpileOnly`"; the script had
  // changed underneath it. Corrected 13.09.2026.)
  //
  // `scripts/` was in exactly the same hole, and worse, because nothing ran
  // it either. `tsconfig.json` includes `src/**` only, so `admin-cli.ts` —
  // which mints the `scrypt$N$r$p$salt$hash` password hash the sign-in path
  // has to parse — was compiled by no project at all. Its only check was an
  // operator running it against a live database during a lockout, which is
  // the worst possible moment to discover a type error, and a drift that
  // silently minted a hash the login path cannot verify would not even be a
  // type error there. It belongs here rather than in `tsconfig.json`: the root
  // project sets `rootDir: "./src"` and is what `tsconfig.build.json` extends,
  // so widening THAT include makes `nest build` try to emit `scripts/` into
  // `dist/` and fail on `rootDir`. This project already has `rootDir: "."`,
  // already has `noEmit`, already runs in CI (`npm run typecheck:test`), and
  // is already the place where "everything the build excludes" is checked.
  // Nothing else reads this file, so nothing else changes.
  //
  // ESLint does not follow: `eslint.config.mjs` ignores `scripts/**`, and the
  // per-file `languageOptions.parserOptions.project` block is scoped to
  // `src/**/*.ts`. So this adds the compiler and no lint rules — which is the
  // right split for a standalone `#!/usr/bin/env node` tool that deliberately
  // uses `console.log` as its user interface and would trip `no-console` on
  // nearly every line.
  //
  // `rootDir` is widened to the package root because the specs live beside
  // `src/`, not under it. `noEmit` keeps this a checker and nothing else.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "test/**/*", "scripts/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "web"]
}
